url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-05-06T11:37:26Z","updated_at":"2014-05-06T11:37:26Z","body":"Hi Christophe,\n\nThe **ANDROID_API** define does not refer to the ndk version. It refers to the Android API Level of the NDK. All versions of the ndk contain interfaces for api levels 3 - 19. In our project we are targeting api level 9. Most games target api level 9. \n\nTL:DR: It's not the right define :).\n\nTo be honest I don't think that supporting older versions of the NDK make sense. The NDK is very unstable and for every release they fix a lot of important bugs. I think that most people who use the NDK, if not all, use the bleeding edge version. \n\nThank you,\nJohan\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/42292268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"JohanKnutzen","id":951311,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1MTMxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/951311?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen","html_url":"https://github.com/JohanKnutzen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanKnutzen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc